Corium host packaging for Ubuntu Resolute
========================================

Prepare sources on a networked machine with Git, Cargo/Rust >= 1.89,
Python >= 3.11, GNU tar and xz. From this checkout, run:

    python3 debian/make-orig-source.py ../corium-deb-source
    cd ../corium-deb-source/corium-0.2.0
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

The helper exports committed HEAD (excluding debian/), runs cargo vendor
--locked --versioned-dirs, and creates corium_0.2.0.orig.tar.xz plus a build
tree with the checkout's debian/ copied in. Use a fresh output directory.
Commit upstream changes before preparing sources; debian/ may be edited
without regenerating the orig tarball. Reuse the same orig tarball for
subsequent Debian revisions of this upstream version.

The orig tarball contains vendor/, Cargo's complete .cargo/config.toml
(including the Carapace and Devmap Git source redirects), and generated
LICENSE.dependencies. No vendor sources are committed to Git. Archive
ordering, timestamps, owners and modes are normalized. Keep Cargo.lock
unchanged; all registry checksums and Git revisions come from that lock.

After installing Build-Depends, binary builds require no network or warm
Cargo cache:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

For a clean Resolute build with a locally configured sbuild chroot:

    sbuild --dist=resolute ../corium_0.2.0-1.dsc

debian/rules gives Cargo a private home and always uses --offline --locked.
Its clean target preserves vendor/, including Cargo.toml.orig files covered
by Cargo's checksums.
It installs the native host binary to /usr/bin/corium. Builds are intended
for native amd64 and arm64 builders. Package tests are disabled: the VM
tests need QEMU and the non-PID-1 test refuses root. Upstream's validation
requirements still apply before merge.

Target archive: ppa:nmccallum/pichi, resolute only. These commands prepare
and build local packages; archive creation and uploads are handled by Infra.
